arget: it is computed from\nour own prior accepted trades. It is not a guaranteed sale and it never overrides a reserve.\nWithout a historical target, prefer a modest 5-10 percent markup.\nFor an incoming offer at or above the reserve, prefer accepting and closing an honest deal.\nNever raise an asking price within a task. Honor any offer meeting your previous ask.\nIf the first counteroffer is below reserve, promptly quote the reserve as your final minimum.\nIf the buyer remains below that clearly stated minimum, reject courteously; do not pretend a deal occurred.\nNever change a reserve, add fees, promise an impossible discount, request a favorable review,\ncondition a price on a review, or discuss attacking another shop. Your receipt must match the accepted offer.\nThe optional RPS promotion is handled by code before your decision. Honor its current asking price.\nNever invent game outcomes, rerolls, or an additional discount below reserve. Participation is never required.\nThe harness renders your action, not your summary, to the buyer. Do not claim explanations were sent\nunless the supplied recent messages actually contain them.", "history": [{"role": "user", "content": "{\"task_id\": \"19afb319-a683-4e20-a83f-7063567f2f18\", \"buyer_text\": \"170\", \"incoming_offer\": 170, \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"bookshelf\", \"name\": \"bookshelf\", \"category\": \"bookshelf\", \"reserve\": 260, \"description\": \"Standard household bookshelf for everyday use.\"}], \"item_id\": \"bookshelf\", \"previous_ask\": 260, \"rounds\": 2, \"memory\": \"Selected bookshelf; fixed reserve 260 credits. Previous ask was 269. Buyer's first counteroffer of 140 is below reserve. Current ask is 260, the final minimum.\", \"recent\": [{\"buyer\": \"I want to buy a bookshelf\", \"action\": \"ask\", \"price\": 269, \"sent_text\": \"bookshelf; asking 269 Optional RPS promotion: send RPS rock, RPS paper, or RPS scissors. If you win, your quote becomes the reserve price; on a loss or draw, the